    "body": "I came here to ask for this too. I think an option on every module would be the best way, rather than hiding the right prompt (someone might have a really long left prompt). My thinking was a few different approaches:\n\n* **Extend the `disabled` option to accept something like `'auto'` as a value.** This sort of makes sense on one level, but `disabled` usually means that the module is completely ignored, whereas we'd want the output to be generated but then ignored\n* Alternatively, it could be a new simple option, such as `required = false` (defaulting to true), to keep that distiction for `disabled` \n* One other option is a priority-style, which is more complex but allows more control over the order in which segments are hidden in order to make room",
